## kick and snare in k-synth

## kick
[
/ 808 Kick — 141->50Hz sweep, 300ms
/ N=13230
N: 13230
T: !N
E: e(T*(0-6.9%N))
/ pitch sweep 141->50Hz
F: 50+91*e(T*(0-60%N))
D: F*((p 2)%(p 0))
P: +\D
S: s P
/ short attack noise thump
Q: e(T*(0-300%N))
R: r T
C: 0.04 f R
W: w (E*S)+(Q*C*.1)
] k! k>d d>r /r 100

## snare

[
/ 808 Snare — 170Hz body dominant, noise tail, 280ms
/ N=12348
N: 12348
T: !N
/ body: 170Hz + 183Hz detuned pair, decay ~20ms
B: e(T*(0-25%N))
F: 170*((p 2)%(p 0))
G: 183*((p 2)%(p 0))
P: +\(N#F)
Q: +\(N#G)
S: B*(s P+s Q)*.5
/ noise tail: full duration — lower in mix than body at start
E: e(T*(0-6.9%N))
R: r T
U: E*R
/ snap
V: e(T*(0-80%N))
K: r T
/ body is primary (*.7), noise secondary (*.4)
W: w (S*.7)+(U*.4)+(V*K*.2)
] k! k>d d>r /r 101
##
v0 w100 a10
v1 w101 a10
